# NOTE: `* text eol=lf` below normalises line endings in everything git does not detect
# as binary, so no compiled or archive file may ever be committed here - it would be
# rewritten. .gitignore keeps __pycache__ out; anything binary that has to be tracked
# needs an explicit `-text` rule of its own.
#
# The thesis repository pins data/*.json by CONTENT HASH, and the runner is Linux.
# Without this, a checkout on Windows would hand the consumer CRLF bytes and the hash
# would not match what was pinned - the file would be "the same file" by name and a
# different one by content.
* text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf
*.py text eol=lf
*.js text eol=lf
*.yml text eol=lf
